  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nSouthwest flow aloft will continue to bring substantial monsoon \nmoisture to most of the area on Friday. Forecast precipitable water \nvalues are near the 80th-90th percentile of normal, indicating a \nhigh potential for heavy rainfall in any showers/thunderstorms that \nform. The best chance looks to be near the Nevada border and high \nterrain in the Central Idaho Mountains with a 50-70% chance of \nprecipitation and a 20-30% chance of thunderstorms on Friday and \nSaturday. With any heavy rainfall that does occur, burn scars and \nsteep/rocky terrain will be susceptible to flash flooding and debris \nflows. Gusty outflow winds up to 35 mph, lightning, and heavy rain \nare the main hazards with these storms. Cooler temperatures will \nalso accompany this push of moisture, with high temperatures about 5-\n10 degrees below normal on Friday and Saturday. \n\nA ridge of high pressure will build back into the region early \nSunday, with lingering moisture keeping a 10-20% chance of \nprecipitation over higher terrain through Monday. A brief warming \nand drying trend will occur on Sunday and Monday ahead of another \npush of showers and thunderstorms with a quick moving low late \nTuesday.",
